B.W8=new A.aX("What has expanded the attack surface according to the passage?",B.MC,1,'The passage states "The shift to remote work has expanded the attack surface dramatically."')
B.PQ=s(["It is expensive","It helps both defenders and attackers","It is unreliable","It replaces human workers"],t.s)
B.Vp=new A.aX('Why is AI described as a "double-edged sword" in cybersecurity?',B.PQ,1,"AI helps detect threats but also enables attackers to craft better attacks.")
B.QZ=s(["Software","Hardware","The human factor","Networks"],t.s)
B.Vs=new A.aX("What is the weakest link in security?",B.QZ,2,'The passage states "The human factor remains the weakest link in any security chain."')
B.MB=s(["Normal patterns","Unusual deviations","Computer viruses","Security updates"],t.s)
B.W0=new A.aX('The word "anomalies" means:',B.MB,1,'"Anomalies" refers to things that deviate from what is standard or expected.')
B.Ok=s([B.W8,B.Vp,B.Vs,B.W0],t.hB)
B.Wp=new A.eA("Cybersecurity in the Modern Age","In an era where virtually every aspect of our lives has a digital component, cybersecurity has emerged as one of the most critical challenges facing individuals, organizations, and governments alike. The frequency and sophistication of cyberattacks continue to escalate, with ransomware, phishing, and data breaches making headlines almost daily.\n\nThe shift to remote work has expanded the attack surface dramatically. Employees accessing corporate networks from home Wi-Fi connections, often on personal devices, have created vulnerabilities that cybercriminals are eager to exploit. A single compromised password can provide access to an entire organization's sensitive data.\n\nArtificial intelligence is proving to be a double-edged sword in cybersecurity. While AI-powered tools can detect anomalies and respond to threats faster than human analysts, the same technology enables attackers to craft more convincing phishing emails and develop malware that can evade traditional detection methods.\n\nThe human factor remains the weakest link in any security chain. Studies consistently show that social engineering attacks\u2014manipulating people into revealing confidential information\u2014account for a significant majority of successful breaches. This underscores the importance of ongoing security awareness training for all employees.\n\nGovernments worldwide are responding with stricter data protection regulations. The European Union's GDPR and similar legislation in other jurisdictions have imposed substantial penalties for organizations that fail to protect personal data adequately, creating a financial incentive for better security practices.","Technology",B.Ok)
